@page "/render/server"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>InteractiveServer Render Mode</PageTitle>

<h1>InteractiveServer Render Mode</h1>

<p>
    This page uses <code>@@rendermode InteractiveServer</code>. The UI is rendered on the server and remains interactive
    via SignalR after initial render.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Why this mode is chosen:</strong>
    Choose <code>InteractiveServer</code> when you want smaller client payloads, centralized state, and live server-driven rendering.
    It is ideal when browser compatibility or server-side access to secure resources is more important than reducing round trips.
</p>

<p>
    <strong>Best cases:</strong>
    admin dashboards, internal business apps, and forms that require server-side validation or high security with minimal client download.
</p>

